    "className": "language-markdown"
  }, "What are the authors proposing?\n")), mdx("p", null, "Proposed Solution: mBLIP\nKey Insight:\nImage encoding is inherently language-agnostic. Once an image encoder is aligned with one LLM, it can be re-aligned with another multilingual LLM using minimal data.\nMethodology:\nRe-alignment Strategy: Take a pretrained image encoder fine-tuned for English and re-align it with a multilingual LLM (e.g., one trained on diverse languages) using machine-translated examples from 95 languages.\nEfficiency: Avoid expensive full pretraining by using ~2.5 million images and 124 million parameters, runnable on consumer-grade hardware.\nBootstrap from Scratch: Combine recent advances in multimodal learning to build the model without relying on pretrained multilingual text encoders.\nPerformance:\nOutperforms state-of-the-art English-only Vision-LLMs (e.g., Llava 1.5) on benchmarks like IGLUE and XM3600."), mdx("h4", {
