    parentName: "ol"
  }, "English-Centric Limitation\nProblem: Current Vision-LLMs (e.g., LiLAVA 1.5) rely exclusively on English data and pretraining, ignoring multilingual coverage. Multilingual pretraining requires expensive end-to-end training using limited multilingual image-text data supplemented with text-only corpora.\nMotivation: The authors argue that image encoding is inherently language-agnostic. Once an image encoder is aligned with one LLM, it can be re-aligned with any multilingual LLM (not just English-centric ones) using minimal data."), mdx("li", {
    parentName: "ol"
