    parentName: "ol"
  }, "Gap in Cross-Lingual Performance\nProblem: Existing multilingual Vision-LLMs (e.g., PaLI-X) underperform English-only models like LiLAVA 1.5 in non-English contexts.\nMotivation: They aim to demonstrate that re-aligning an English-aligned encoder with a multilingual LLM (instead of training from scratch) yields competitive or better performance across tasks (captioning, reasoning, QA) and languages.\nCore Motivation Summary\nThe authors seek to democratize multilingual Vision-LLMs by:\nReducing dependency on expensive pretraining via re-alignment.\nLeveraging multilingual LLMs to achieve cross-lingual capabilities.\nEnabling efficient training on accessible hardware (e.g., consumer GPUs).\nClosing the performance gap between English and multilingual Vision-LLMs.\nTheir goal is to create a scalable, cost-effective, and multilingually inclusive framework for vision-and-language tasks.")), mdx("h4", {
